{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Only My Sabbaths you shall keep</b> — even though you are pressed with urgency in the work, do not set aside the Sabbath on its account. Any 'akhin ve-rakin (אַכִין וְרַקִּין) is a restrictive limitation, to exclude the Sabbath from the work of the Tabernacle. This is the language of Rashi. And it does not seem correct to me, for according to the midrash of our Sages, 'akhin ve-rakin limits the observance of the Sabbath, for restrictive limitations in their view everywhere restrict that which is commanded, and if you interpret the limitation as referring to the matter of the work of the Tabernacle, it would be permitted to do that work on the Sabbath. Rather, this limitation is for circumcision or for saving a life and similar cases, which override the Sabbath. And thus they said in tractate Yoma (Jerusalemite 8:5): From where do we derive that a doubtful case of life-and-death overrides the Sabbath? Rabbi Abbahu said in the name of Rabbi Yohanan: 'Only אֶת שַׁבְּתֹתַי תִּשְׁמֹרוּ' — a limitation. And the work of the Tabernacle, which does not override the Sabbath — because He warned concerning it here. And according to the plain sense (peshat) it is so: it says, you shall do the work of the Tent of Meeting, but My Sabbaths you shall keep forever. And in Torat Kohanim (Leviticus 11:30): One might think that the building of the Temple overrides the Sabbath — Scripture says, 'אֶת שַׁבְּתֹתַי תִּשְׁמֹרוּ וּמִקְדָּשִׁי תִּירָאוּ אֲנִי ה''. And the reason for 'My Sabbaths' — because the Sabbaths of the year are many.\n\nAnd by way of truth, He commanded here concerning זָכוֹר (remember) and שָׁמוֹר (observe), as I hinted in their secret (Ramban on Exodus 20:8). And this is the reason for 'My Sabbaths,' and He said regarding both of them 'כִּי אוֹת הִיא' (for it is a sign), for it is 'between Me and you' to know. And He said 'וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם אֶת הַשַּׁבָּת,' and imposed the punishment of כָּרֵת (excision) upon its desecrators (Exodus 31:14), for the spirit returns to Elohim who gave it (Ecclesiastes 12:7), and this shall be cut off from there. And He said, concerning the seventh day, that it is שַׁבַּת שַׁבָּתוֹן קֹדֶשׁ לַה' (a sabbath of solemn rest, holy to YHWH) (Exodus 31:15), because it is the Foundation of the World. And He mentioned concerning the Sabbath that it is בְּרִית עוֹלָם (an everlasting covenant) (Exodus 31:16), and returned and said, כִּי אוֹת הִיא בֵּינִי וּבֵין בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל (for it is a sign between Me and between the children of Israel) (Exodus 31:17) — the sign is the Sabbath on the seventh day, and the reason is that the day is a sign and the Sabbath is a sign forever. And this is the reason for 'שָׁבַת וַיִּנָּפַשׁ' (He rested and was refreshed), and it is the נְשָׁמָה יְתֵרָה (additional soul) (Beitzah 16a) that comes from the Foundation of the World, in whose hand is the נֶפֶשׁ (soul) of every living thing (Job 12:10). And behold, the pericope is elucidated. And I have already hinted at its matter in the Decalogue (Ramban on Exodus 32:28). And the enlightened will understand."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "Ramban's cross-reference at the end appears to cite Exodus 32:28, but he likely intends his comment on Exodus 20:8 (the Sabbath in the Decalogue); the cited location may reflect a variant or copyist error in the tradition."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:19:43.462185831Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}